@startuml SequenceSmartMatch
title Sequence Diagram — SmartMatch Algorithm
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Student as S
participant "Frontend\n(Next.js)" as FE
participant "Backend\n(Express)" as BE
participant "SmartMatch\nEngine" as SM
database "PostgreSQL\n(Neon)" as DB

S -> FE : Enable SmartMatch mode
FE -> BE : GET /api/matching?limit=10\n(Authorization: Bearer token)
BE -> BE : requireAuth\nExtract userId from JWT

BE -> DB : SELECT student\n(skills[], department)\nWHERE userId = ?
DB --> BE : Student profile

BE -> DB : SELECT user.university
DB --> BE : University name

BE -> DB : SELECT active offers\n+ company data (name, logo,\nindustry, location)
DB --> BE : Offers list[]

BE -> SM : getSmartMatches(userId, limit)

loop For each offer
  SM -> SM : **norm()**: lowercase, remove\nnon-alphanumeric (keep +#),\ncollapse spaces
  SM -> SM : **tokenize()**: split into\nwords > 1 character

  SM -> SM : **1. Skills Match (50%)**\nFor each student skill vs\nrequirements + description:\n- Exact match: weight 1.0\n- Partial (>=50% word overlap):\n  weight 0.7 x overlap ratio\nNormalize by min(requirements count,\nstudent skills count)

  SM -> SM : **2. Department Relevance (25%)**\nMap department to keywords\n(17 department mappings:\nCS → software/web/data/ai/cloud...\nIT → network/system/web...\nEE → electronics/iot/embedded...)\nCount keyword hits in offer text\nAmplify x 1.5

  SM -> SM : **3. Location Proximity (15%)**\nExtract city from university name\nCity found in offer/company\nlocation → 1.0\nRemote offer → 0.7\nNo match → 0.1

  SM -> SM : **4. Title Relevance (10%)**\nSkill words found in offer title\nNormalize by min(skill count, 3)

  SM -> SM : **Final Score =**\n(0.50 x skillScore)\n+ (0.25 x deptScore)\n+ (0.15 x locationScore)\n+ (0.10 x titleScore)\nx 100
end

SM --> BE : MatchedOffer[] sorted by\nscore descending, limited to N

BE --> FE : {matches[]: id, title,\ndescription, requirements,\nduration, location, type,\nbannerUrl, companyName,\ncompanyLogoUrl, companyIndustry,\ncompanyLocation, matchScore,\nmatchedSkills[]}

FE --> S : Display recommended offers\nwith compatibility score

@enduml
